  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-henkel">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Henkel</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2015–2018 · Associate Manager, Revenue Management</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Built the store-level allocation model behind Dial's $0.93 EDLP launch at Walmart, matching each store's weekly sell-through to shelf capacity, driving 300%+ revenue growth. When Walmart's buyer pushed back on shipment volumes, walked them through the model and secured agreement, then partnered with supply chain to prioritize top sell-through stores; the price investment earned 7 endcaps for the year.</li>
      <li>Drove $55MM in profit across key retail accounts with assortment, pricing, and promotion strategies grounded in price-elasticity modeling.</li>
      <li>Stood up Henkel's Canadian Revenue Management function from the ground up.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-advantage">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Advantage Sales &amp; Marketing</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2014–2015 · Category Analyst → Category Manager</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Managed weekly performance reporting and Walmart/Sam's Club sales pitch decks for ~15 CPG clients at once, aimed at growing their distribution.</li>
      <li>Promoted to embedded consultant for Sargento and Church &amp; Dwight: their day-to-day analytics partner on store-level product and category performance across Walmart's U.S. footprint, turning findings into the recommendations they took to Walmart and Sam's Club buyers to win merchandising and placement decisions.</li>
    </ul>
